{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1507009-nuwisha-and-ananasi","id":1507009,"title":"Nuwisha and Ananasi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-30T19:14:23-07:00","id":1507009,"title":"Nuwisha and Ananasi","content":"I like the ideas of both species, although I have nothing against the other, because I haven't seen them all yet, but I intend to, eventually, anyway, in the books of both races instructions are given on how to make one ready-to-play character, but their concepts seem more suitable for NPCs, which brings me to the question. Does anyone here have experience with playing as one of these species?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T19:48:49-07:00","id":1507011,"title":"","content":"Nuwisha are the harder of the two in my mind. Part of this is that North America doesn't have a Fera-coalition for them to be part of, and the most likely groups from them to interact with are the Corax and Garou, which means a lot of conceptual overlap. Despite the fact that real coyotes are highly social animals like most canines, the books treat the Nuwisha more as loners which doesn't help. I'd only really suggest them as PCs in game with a small number of players, and no Ragabash if Garou are being played.<br /> <br /> I've had much better experiences with the Ananasi because there's just more options with what to do with them. It's easier to come up with 4-6 concepts that can all work together without anyone feeling like they're duplicating. It's a very different sort of game from most WtA play, but it works. They can be pretty awkward to fit into mixed Fera games because of their separation from the rest, but it works with a group that's designed to be open to their peculiarities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T19:54:33-07:00","id":1507013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1507009-nuwisha-and-ananasi?p=1507011#post1507011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nuwisha are the harder of the two in my mind. Part of this is that North America doesn't have a Fera-coalition for them to be part of, and the most likely groups from them to interact with are the Corax and Garou, which means a lot of conceptual overlap. Despite the fact that real coyotes are highly social animals like most canines, the books treat the Nuwisha more as loners which doesn't help. I'd only really suggest them as PCs in game with a small number of players, and no Ragabash if Garou are being played.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you define smal numbers of players, I only ever played within a group of 4 or 5 counting with the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T20:57:31-07:00","id":1507015,"title":"","content":"My experience has been that Nuwisha worked best in games with maybe 2 or 3 PCs and a Storyteller. The alternative is what I came to refer to as &quot;Pariah&quot; games, which is to say ones involving Caitiff vampires, Ronin werewolves, Orphan mages, and the like (Ghouls, Sorcerers, Psychics, Mummies, etc.). Also, I've found that their inherently chaotic nature means that they often work well in games with a similar feel to things like Fear &amp; Loathing in Las Vegas, From Dusk til Dawn, Once Upon a Time in Mexico, Smokin' Aces, and Crank (and its sequel, High Voltage). Or perhaps the second or third Saints Row video game. <br /> <br /> Ananasi have the weird issue of, by nature of being the only non-vertebrate shifters, having a mindset and world view that is the most alien to humans. Even the ultra-primitive savagery of the Rokea is more understandable. I tend to approach them as being very detached from humanity, seeing others more as tools and props than actual people. In that sense, they're probably among the more horrific of the changing breeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T22:20:30-07:00","id":1507020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1507009-nuwisha-and-ananasi?p=1507013#post1507013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you define smal numbers of players, I only ever played within a group of 4 or 5 counting with the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like NOoC said, 2-3 players and the ST","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T00:26:42-07:00","id":1507026,"title":"","content":"I haven't played either, but I ST a long-running chronicle with an Ananasi Kumoti Viskr. It's a mixed-splat (two sorcerers, one Stargazer, one Ananasi) group and the spider fits into the dynamic pretty comfortably. That said, although it's not quite the Pariah group <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> mentioned, all are loner-types and Kumoti Viskr is probably the most sociable Ananasi option. It probably really depends on the characters how well it works, but that's true for any group.<br /> <br /> The weirdness of the Ananasi is going to relax somewhat during the course of the chronicle, and that's ok imo. The player is human after all, and if they are going to integrate into a group, there needs to be some flexibility. Again, this probably depends on the Aspect. Tenere and Hatar NPCs I played were very different.<br /> <br /> There are also some mechanical quirks that need to be addressed with Ananasi (most of them related to Crawlerling form), but once the kinks are ironed out, they are perfectly playable.<br /> <br /> One thing I will mention is to keep in mind that Ananasi in addition to being based on non-vertebrates also cover multiple species, something that doesn't get too much attention in the rules. The different species have different temperaments and unique physicalities to them which should be taken into account, especially because there's an insane diversity of spiders out there. Hunting strategy is a big factor in how they would approach problems. My player is a Salticid, and thus tends to pounce on problems head on. A Deinopis is an ambush predator and would go differently about things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T04:46:11-07:00","id":1507048,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Nuwisha much more than the execution. They tread a lot of the same narrative space as the ragabash, while requiring a lot of meta knowledge of the setting and narrative WHILE still being cooperative and not disruptive to the game.<br /> <br /> I've met relativley few players able to play the Nuwisha without it turning into a bloody mess, and for this reason I either heavily supervise anyone wanting one or just outright decline them for games.<br /> <br /> Ananasi on the other hand are much more playable even if a lot of the other PC's might end up feeling filthy for cooperating with them. Their morals and behavior are downright weird and mismatched in comparison to the other breeds - they are less about personal legendry and doing right by Gaia and more about making things better for themselves and following the sporadic guidance of Ananasa.<br /> <br /> This makes them highly individualistic, but also a boon to most shifter groups as they allow a drastically different perspective and willigness to use tools others would never consider. In some ways they are a way for shifters to use tools that would traditionally be vampire tools.<br /> <br /> For this reason they work well in multiple fera chronicles as well as in all ananasi chronicles. They are more complex and require a level of player maturity - being a sneaky bastard should be firmly in the character teritorry and not inconvenience and make other players uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> We've had amazing Ananasi in our games, including one who was essentially a well connected purveyor of Hearts Desires with a huge reputation and both helped the rest of the cast through his money and connections while gently asking for repayment in building up his Empire.<br /> <br /> The character was amazing and beloved by the cast, but the player was tired of always being confident, cool and in charge fixing problems with influence and money. Now he is a crazy ratkin with an excessive amount of explosives, and his old PC is a NPC <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T20:17:52-07:00","id":1507092,"title":"","content":"I think in theory there shouldn't any problem for Nuwisha to be a PC, especially in a Werewolf chronicle. They have aligned interests and are similar canids. The main issue is per <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a>, they can duplicate a Garou Ragabash so what is the attraction except to be &quot;special&quot;? It certainly can be justified, but I think it is a fair question for the ST and other Players to ask, &quot;Why do you need to Nuwisha instead of just playing a Ragabash?&quot; On the other hand, there certainly are a lot of valid Garou Ragabash concepts that don't really fit Nuwisha, and some Nuwisha concepts that might not fit the normal role of a Ragabash.<br /> <br /> However, in practice, there are some players who choose to play Nuwisha for the same reason some players want to play a Malkavian vampire, a Kender, or any Chaotic Neutral characters - they just want to act out regardless of whether it disrupts the game, and they have the excuse it is because their concept requires/excuses it. The problem is not that a Nuwisha is in the game. The problem is that these players are being disruptive and will lean to any concept that allows them to do that.<br /> <br /> As an ST, I do like to have them as an NPC in chronicles where it makes sense that there'd be a Nuwisha presence. I feel I can utilize their strengths but not disrupt the game with their antics.<br /> <br /> I have never played an Ananasi or seen one played. I'm not fond of the concept actually as written. So when I ST, they don't exist in the setting although I do have a spider themed fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T02:11:20-07:00","id":1507102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1507009-nuwisha-and-ananasi#post1507009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Does anyone here have experience with playing as one of these species?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nuwisha I have not as they're not overly present in the places I run most of my chronicles.<br /> <br /> Ananasi we've had a number of PCs over the decades in our chronicles:<br /> <br /> - In one of our northern Oceania chronicles we had a Kumoti Wyrsta who conducted themselves as a guardian of knowledge and life modelling themselves on Areop-Enap of their homeland, Nauru.<br /> <br /> - A vicious nasty brute modelled on <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Mararan</span>\u200b, a Hatar Myrmidon who still believed in the struggles of his people that he had fought for before coming into his Ananasi inheritance. He was pretty much the Ahroun of the group.<br /> <br /> - Auntie Pearl, a Kumatai Elder who runs a community group in the Tanami Desert, spending most of her time in Yuendumu. She has a strong familial and spiritual bond with the Ancestor, Mamupururnpa Jukurrpa\u200b.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}